# B2B SaaS Overlay

- Every tenant-owned row carries `tenantId`; every query is scoped by it. Enforce in a repository base or database row-level security, never ad hoc in handlers.
- Resolve tenant from the authenticated session, never from a client-supplied header or body field.
- RBAC: roles map to permissions; code checks permissions (`can("invoice:write")`), not role names.
- Plan entitlements and feature flags are checked in the application layer through one `entitlements` service.
- Subscription lifecycle (trialing, active, past_due, canceled) is an explicit state machine driven by provider webhooks.
- Webhook handlers verify signatures, are idempotent (store processed event IDs), and respond quickly.
- Write an append-only audit log entry (`actorId`, `tenantId`, action, target, timestamp) for every security-relevant or admin action.
- Provide tenant-level export and deletion paths; avoid cross-tenant joins in analytics code.
